    "prose": "Rain rattled across the covered yard as Aya and Mert faced the wide workshop gate. The same restored mosaic panel stayed raised between them, each supporting one side.\n\n“Together,” Mert said.\n\nAya tightened her hold without pulling ahead. “Together.”\n\nThey carried the panel through the wide workshop gate into the covered yard in one coordinated crossing, keeping their shared hold steady and the fragile mosaic level between them.\n\nA gust drove rain past the edge of the covering. The sound made Aya want to hurry toward the ramp, but Mert’s steps remained measured. For one pace, she moved faster than he did, and the panel’s edge began to angle.\n\nAya caught herself before the tilt grew. She slowed to Mert’s pace, matching each careful step while maintaining her side of their shared carry. The panel settled level again, still intact.\n\nMert watched the change in her movement. His gaze went from her feet to the even line of the panel, and some of the tension left his face.\n\n“That pace works,” he said.\n\nAya nodded. Her arms ached, and rain hammered harder nearby, but she did not try to take the lead. “Keep it steady. I’ll stay with you.”\n\nThey remained together in the covered yard, both hands still supporting the mosaic. The level covered ramp waited ahead, but neither of them started onto it. For now, they held their position and kept the restored panel balanced safely between them.",
